  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 7,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.05,
            0.432,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.846,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The prime factorisation of 30 has only one 2. So, the largest common subpart should contain only one 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.127,
            0.464,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How many 3s will it contain?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.145,
            0.847,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The prime factorisation of 30 has only one 3. So, the largest common subpart should contain only one 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.183,
            0.495,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This has been carried out below."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.21,
            0.584,
            0.27
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{array} { l } 3 0 = \\boxed 2 \\times \\boxed 3 \\times 5 \\\\ 7 2 = \\boxed 2 \\times \\boxed 2 \\times \\boxed 3 \\times 3 \\end{array}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.369,
            0.276,
            0.518,
            0.295
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{HCF} = 2 \\times 3 = 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.307,
            0.849,
            0.366
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, to find the HCF, we identify the common primes and find the the given numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.374,
            0.553,
            0.398
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 5: Find the HCF of 225 and 750."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.411,
            0.405,
            0.621,
            0.45
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}225 &= 3 \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 5 \\\\750 &= 2 \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 5 \\times 5\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.459,
            0.846,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Common primes: 3 and 5. Let us find the largest common subpart. How many 3s will it contain?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.497,
            0.846,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "750 contains only one 3, which is the minimum number of 3 across both numbers. So the largest common subpart should contain only one 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.536,
            0.442,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How many 5s will it contain?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.555,
            0.615,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "225 contains the minimum number of 5s which occurs two times. So, the largest common subpart should contain two "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{fs}, \\mathrm{i.e.}, 5 \\times 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.656,
            0.536,
            0.864,
            0.594
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{array} { l } 2 2 5 = 3 \\times \\boxed 3 \\times \\boxed 5 \\times \\boxed 5 \\\\ 7 5 0 = 2 \\times \\boxed 3 \\times \\boxed 5 \\times \\boxed 5 \\times 5 \\end{array}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.653,
            0.6,
            0.844,
            0.62
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{HCF} = 3 \\times 5 \\times 5 = 75"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.634,
            0.847,
            0.674
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To find the HCF of more than 2 numbers, a similar method of finding the largest common subpart of the common primes can be followed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.684,
            0.316,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.711,
            0.6,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the HCF of the following numbers: (a) 24, 180 (b) 42, 75, 24 (c) 240, 378 (d) 400, 2500 (e) 300, 800"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.816,
            0.848,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Consider the numbers 72 and 144. Suppose they are factorised into composite numbers as: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 2 = 6 \\times 1 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 4 4 = 8 \\times 1 8 ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Seeing this, can one say that these two numbers have no common factor other than 1? Why not?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.934,
            0.187,
            0.949
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "54"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
